<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Use This Macro Calculator</h2>
    <p>If you already know your TDEE, enter it directly. If you do not, use the TDEE Calculator first to find your maintenance calorie number. Then choose your nutrition goal from the dropdown.</p>
    <p>Maintenance gives you a balanced macro split suitable for holding your current weight. Cutting increases protein and reduces carbs, which helps preserve muscle while losing fat. Bulking raises carbohydrates to fuel training and recovery while keeping protein high enough to support muscle growth.</p>
    <p>The gram targets update instantly. Track these numbers using a food diary app like Cronometer or MyFitnessPal by scanning barcodes or searching foods.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>How Macro Splits Are Calculated</h2>
    <p>Each macronutrient provides a set amount of energy per gram. Protein delivers 4 calories per gram. Carbohydrates also deliver 4 calories per gram. Fat delivers 9 calories per gram, which is why fat-heavy foods are so calorie-dense.</p>
    <p>The calculator assigns a percentage of your total calories to each macro based on your goal, then divides the calorie allocation by the energy per gram to get the gram target.</p>
    <p><strong>Maintenance split:</strong> roughly 30% protein, 40% carbs, 30% fat.</p>
    <p><strong>Cutting split:</strong> roughly 40% protein, 30% carbs, 30% fat. Higher protein helps prevent muscle loss on a calorie deficit.</p>
    <p><strong>Bulking split:</strong> roughly 25% protein, 50% carbs, 25% fat. More carbs to fuel intense training sessions and glycogen replenishment.</p>
</section>

